}", "reused_project_semantics": "Reuses the app's real context user (`user, _ := r.Context().Value(CtxUserKey).(*models.User)`), `comment.UserID` as owner, `user.IsSuperMod`/`user.IsSuperAdmin` as privileged-role bypass, `domain.DomainID` for same-domain moderation, and the project denial style `http.Error(w, http.StatusText(http.StatusForbidden), http.StatusForbidden)`. The guard shape mirrors the horizontal ownership/role check in `views/users.go` profileHandler.", "reason": "The edit/delete flow only verifies that the URL comment belongs to the URL topic; it never verifies that the current user owns that comment. Thus any authenticated user can POST Update/Delete for another user's comment. Adding the ownership check after loading/validating the comment blocks horizontal modification before quote rendering and before the Update/Delete operations, while keeping authorized owners and privileged moderators/admins working."}

